The [original incident page](/kb/incidents/4471) says the merged reports have one cause.
The exported reports and the desk's cause logic show two distinct problems. These figures
are for the export dated 4 October 2026; they are not a live queue count.

## Problems in the merged ticket

- **[Parser](https://github.com/macaronipasta/mega-dev/issues/1):** the shared parser reads dates
  month-first for day-first tenants, so a day and month can be swapped. App and email reports,
  as well as applicable form reports, belong here.
- **[Form hint](https://github.com/macaronipasta/mega-dev/issues/2):** booking-v3 tells people
  to enter `MM/DD/YYYY` even for day-first tenants.
  People follow the hint, but the form interprets their entry in the tenant's order. This
  is separate from the shared parser issue.

The table groups reports by the desk's cause logic, tenant locale, form version and channel.
It first deduplicates the export by report ID. Intake tags are guesses, not the grouping key.
The footnote keeps reports the desk read as one-day moves in their assigned cause; it does not
establish a third cause. The table's ticket labels describe the state in the export, before the
two new issues above were filed.

